<div class="guide-styles" data-ay-injected="true" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's long awaited Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Blood Death Knight Tanks in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. We are finally into the most anticipated tier of the expansion, coming face to face with World of Warcrafts most famous antagonist, The Lich King Arthas Menethil himself. Icecrown Citadel is a raid where you see Blizzard experiment with new mechanics, and there is a few fights where they're quite punishing. <br/>
<br/>The power jump from ToGC to Ice Crown is quite noticeable, with better optimized gear than seen in previous tiers and stat power creep. Like previous tiers, there are a lot of options in slots incase you don't get your bis, but below you'll find 2 gear sets for the hardest content in the tier. We're approaching gear a bit different this time around, instead of focusing on pure Estimated Health Pool (EHP) over all else, we're focusing on Theck-Meloree Index (TMI). These numbers are generated using the Blood Death Knight Tank sim found <a href="https://wowsims.github.io/wotlk/tank_deathknight/#" target="_blank">here</a> (Shout out to RaiN and Jooper for their work on the sim) each sim below is using the settings posted by Char in the Blight Club discord <a href="https://discord.com/channels/894792866658930688/1148883400967594054" target="_blank">here</a>. TMI is a metric developed to calculate the threat of spike damage, and then quantify the smoothness of your damage intake based on that spike damage and frequency. The lower the TMI, the higher chance of you living. TMI is a more accurate measure of your ability to survive than Chance of Death since Chance of Death measures the tail end of your iterations and not the average. I know that's a lot to take in, but if you take anything from this rambling is that these sets are designed to give you the best chance at living in each of these fights. This is another tier where gearing your tanks up will be #1 priority so have fun, and good luck!<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Blood Death Knight Tanks in Phase 4</h2>As stated above, the EHP above all else rule of thumb is not our ultimate deciding factor here - but it still plays an exceptionally important role. We're dropping a lot of Parry from ToGC and gaining a lot of dodge - we love to see that. Along with that we get an abundance of hit and expertise you should have no problems in that regard. <br/>
<br/>
