<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="ruby-sanctum">Updates for Best in Slot Gear in Ruby Sanctum</h3>
<a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=39863/halion">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Halion</span></a> is our final boss of Wrath of the Lich King, and being a single boss, there's not a lot of loot changes coming up. First, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54579/treads-of-impending-resurrection">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Treads of Impending Resurrection</span></a> is a small upgrade over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50625/grinning-skull-greatboots">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Grinning Skull Greatboots</span></a>. Providing 44 more Armor, 42 more Strength, 26 more Stamina, double blue sockets for the extra 9 Stamina socket bonus. However, due to having 22 less Defense, and 14 less Dodge Rating - you will see a decrease in avoidance. On top of losing the large 61 Expertise rating dropping you roughly from 24 Expertise to 17. These still come out ahead in terms of survivability, but the difference here in relatively small in terms of Chance to Die and TMI. <br/>
<br/>Second we have <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54591/petrified-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Petrified Twilight Scale</span></a>, and while it provides 448 more armor than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a>, the equip effect for Dodge Rating doesn't outweigh the Stamina from the latter. It's still a decently strong trinket if you haven't been able to get your hands on any of the other bis trinkets, and it's nice to have options.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Frost for Blood Death Knight Tanks in Phase 4</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> become the new currency for phase 4. These emblems will hold their important for weeks after release, incentivizing people to play and do lower end content just to get these. In order to get the highest tier pieces, you'll need to first buy the tier with emblems which will require A LOT of them. You can earn 109 Emblems per week, except from the first week where you can only earn 105. 25 from each ICC raid size, 2 from each VoA raid size, 35 from Daily Heroic+++, 10 from the weekly raid, and 10 from the weekly ICC raid quest. <br/>
<br/>
<b>
<ins>Tier costs:</ins></b>
<br/>Helm: 95 <br/>Shoulders: 60<br/>Chest: 95<br/>Gloves: 60<br/>Pants: 95<br/>
<b>Total: 405</b>
<br/>
<br/>Some of these tier pieces won't be major upgrades over your 25-man Heroic ToGC loot - and their upgradability will be determined based on if you are able to get your hands on <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52028/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_judgementsofthejust.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a>. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> drops from ICC 10-man Heroic, and 25-man Normal. You need one of these marks to upgrade your emblem bought 251 ilvl tier to 264 Tier. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52028/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_judgementsofthejust.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> drop from only 25-man Heroic, and allows you to upgrade your 264 ilvl tier to 277 tier. <br/>
<br/>Due to the new nature of this path to tier, the list below may not be accurate for you. If you're able to upgrade a tier piece first, that would be my suggestion. The quicker you get to 4pc, the better. Aside from the strong 4pc bonus, these tier pieces range from pretty equal, to significantly better than other items in the slots<br/>
