<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinket options for Blood Death Knight Tanks in Phase 4</h3>We have 3 options which come out ahead of all others, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50364/sindragosas-flawless-fang">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Flawless Fang</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a>. While <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a> looks amazing, its worth noting a few things. Currently this trinket sims at 80% uptime, but you uptime is dependent upon tank swaps and tanking time. The other thing to take note is that depending on how long you're tanking, you're not going to see max stacks - more like 5 or so between tank swaps. Which still comes out to 108/<wbr/>135 Stamina and 2128 Armor. Very good. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> is our last bis option, lets look at the reasoning below.<br/>
<br/>The other thing I want to talk about is trinket alternatives, particularly between <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a>. Just comparing these at quick glance, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a> seems like the winner, right? More Stamina, an a higher number on the On Use than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a>. You need to look at this a different way though. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a> is a flat damage absorb, not bad at all, and can definitely help you save you in a bad situation. The usefulness of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> must not go understated, this provides a flat health increase, when timed right can cover a Soul Reaper cast, a tick, and a Frenzy window. This balloons this value substantially, and the best performing trinket for  Sindragosa and very close for Lich King survivability. It just takes some thinking ahead.  <br/>
<br/>With the addition of  <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=39863/halion">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Halion</span></a>, we get another decent option Trinket, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54591/petrified-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Petrified Twilight Scale</span></a>. and while it provides 448 more armor than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a>, the equip effect for Dodge Rating doesn't outweigh the Stamina from the latter. It's still a decently strong trinket if you haven't been able to get your hands on any of the other bis trinkets, and it's nice to have options.<div class="pad"></div>
